[INFO] Step 1. MDTs Recruitment

Group 1 - Initial Assessment Team (IAT)
  👨‍⚕️ Member 1 (Emergency Medicine Physician): Acute care and initial diagnostics
  👨🏻‍⚕️ Member 2 (Psychiatrist): Mental health disorders and differential diagnoses
  👩🏼‍⚕️ Member 3 (General Practitioner): Primary care and psychosomatic conditions

Group 2 - Gastroenterology Team (GET)
  👨‍⚕️ Member 1 (Gastroenterologist): Expertise in gastrointestinal disorders
  👨🏻‍⚕️ Member 2 (Dietitian): Nutritional assessment and gastrointestinal health
  👩🏼‍⚕️ Member 3 (Infectious Disease Specialist): Evaluation for infectious causes of gastrointestinal symptoms

Group 3 - Pain Management Team (PMT)
  👨‍⚕️ Member 1 (Pain Management Specialist): Chronic pain assessment and management
  👨🏻‍⚕️ Member 2 (Clinical Psychologist): Psychological impact of chronic pain
  👩🏼‍⚕️ Member 3 (Physical Therapist): Evaluation of physical functionality and range of motion

Group 4 - Psychosomatic Disorders Team (PDT)
  👨‍⚕️ Member 1 (Psychiatrists specializing in psychosomatic medicine): Evaluation of psychosomatic manifestations
  👨🏻‍⚕️ Member 2 (Behavioral Therapist): Techniques for managing anxiety and somatic symptoms
  👩🏼‍⚕️ Member 3 (Nurse Practitioner): Holistic assessment of physical and psychosocial health

Group 5 - Final Review and Decision Team (FRDT)
  👨‍⚕️ Member 1 (Internal Medicine Specialist): Comprehensive review of physical health and multi-system involvement
  👨🏻‍⚕️ Member 2 (Psychiatrist): Specialist in diagnosing mental health disorders
  👩🏼‍⚕️ Member 3 (Rheumatologist): Assessment for any potential autoimmune or connective tissue disorders contributing to symptoms

